WEBVTT

00:01:31.590 --> 00:01:34.720
Long ago, there lived a
young man who came to live...

00:01:34.790 --> 00:01:37.730
...in the deserted wilds to
escape the gaze of other people.

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:41.730
The man's name was Joe.
Because he hated other people...

00:01:41.970 --> 00:01:44.460
...he moved into
an abandoned tower...

00:01:44.540 --> 00:01:47.940
...and lived with dolls
as his only companions.

00:01:48.570 --> 00:01:53.910
But the man fell in love with
a girl in the village named Anne.

00:01:55.010 --> 00:01:56.780
Such an ironic twist...

00:02:05.090 --> 00:02:08.580
He, a man whose heart had never
connected with another person's!

00:02:08.660 --> 00:02:14.030
But his vexing obsession continued!
He wanted to live together with Anne!

00:02:14.370 --> 00:02:16.490
He thought how happy
he would be if only...

00:02:16.570 --> 00:02:19.230
...he could make her his alone
for the rest of his life!

00:02:19.310 --> 00:02:24.240
A few days later,
the man's wish became reality.

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:27.070
Anne suddenly vanished!

00:02:28.950 --> 00:02:31.820
Are you saying... Did the man?!

00:02:31.880 --> 00:02:35.840
Yes. One day, the villagers,
hoping to take Anne back...

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:38.620
...appeared at Joe's tower.

00:02:38.920 --> 00:02:40.650
And what they saw there...

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:53.340
A marionette of a young girl
who seemed to beg them for help.

00:02:53.670 --> 00:02:55.440
And then...

00:02:55.510 --> 00:02:56.740
HELP ME!!!

00:02:58.140 --> 00:03:01.270
I'm scared!
I'm scared! I'm scared!

00:03:01.780 --> 00:03:05.270
Uh, Amelia? It's just a
story, okay? Just a story!

00:03:05.350 --> 00:03:07.650
Calm down already!

00:03:09.820 --> 00:03:12.350
So? What's the
point of that story?

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:14.150
Well, don't ask me!

00:03:14.230 --> 00:03:16.850
The man's obsession
became the seed for a curse...

00:03:16.930 --> 00:03:19.800
...that sealed the girl's
soul into the puppet!

00:03:19.870 --> 00:03:21.830
Oh, what a beautiful story!

00:03:21.900 --> 00:03:23.370
You mean "What a
creepy story", don't you?!

00:03:23.440 --> 00:03:25.960
Hmpf! If that sort of
story scares you that much...

00:03:26.040 --> 00:03:27.100
...you really are still a little kid!

00:03:27.170 --> 00:03:28.800
What did you say?!

00:03:28.870 --> 00:03:32.280
In that case, YOU must still be a
little kid! Look at your legs!

00:03:35.180 --> 00:03:38.010
Uh... Well... This is...
Leave me alone!

00:03:38.080 --> 00:03:39.110
Don't count on it!

00:03:39.190 --> 00:03:41.350
Please! Please, you two...

00:03:41.420 --> 00:03:43.510
Now, how do you think
a young man was able...

00:03:43.590 --> 00:03:47.120
...to seal a girl's soul
into a puppet's body?

00:03:49.090 --> 00:03:51.530
What if, in the place
he stored all his dolls...

00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:54.620
...he had a copy
of the Claire Bible?

00:03:56.270 --> 00:03:59.000
I can imagine that the magical
power stored in a manuscript...

00:03:59.070 --> 00:04:02.910
...could work with the man's
feelings to do such a thing.

00:04:02.980 --> 00:04:05.310
However... I think you're
just making this all up!

00:04:05.380 --> 00:04:09.540
Oh... Then why don't we
go and see for ourselves?

00:04:10.480 --> 00:04:15.250
To the legendary tower the man lived in.
The accursed Artemay Tower!

00:04:25.560 --> 00:04:30.630
Y- You people aren't
going to that tower, are you?

00:04:31.370 --> 00:04:33.430
Yeah, we are. Why?

00:04:33.510 --> 00:04:38.200
That place is a deathtrap!
If you go, you'll never return!

00:04:38.540 --> 00:04:41.840
You'd better not do this!
Just stop right now!

00:04:43.750 --> 00:04:46.620
Mister, you're scaring me MORE!

00:04:47.590 --> 00:04:49.080
Did he just say?

00:04:49.150 --> 00:04:51.120
We'd never return...

00:04:51.890 --> 00:04:53.380
We scared!

00:04:53.460 --> 00:04:55.720
There's one more thing.

00:04:55.790 --> 00:05:01.360
All those who have gone to the
tower have turned into dolls as well...

00:05:01.600 --> 00:05:02.620
...is what I've heard, anyway.

00:05:02.700 --> 00:05:06.430
All those people who went to take
Anne back would be our enemies.

00:05:06.510 --> 00:05:08.600
What! No way!

00:05:08.840 --> 00:05:11.710
Come on! It's just
a story, after all!

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:16.680
Yeah! And Lina Inverse, the sorcery
genius, has nothing to fear!

00:05:17.080 --> 00:05:19.880
If you say that, then I guess
there's no stopping you.

00:05:19.950 --> 00:05:23.580
But you must take care!

00:05:23.660 --> 00:05:27.890
If you insist on going, then let
me give you something useful.

00:05:30.860 --> 00:05:32.830
Take this when you go!

00:05:34.630 --> 00:05:36.290
Wh- What is it?

00:05:41.270 --> 00:05:43.300
Oh, we finally made it!

00:05:43.380 --> 00:05:45.500
We didn't have
to wait until morning.

00:05:45.580 --> 00:05:49.210
Yes, we did. Those two refused
to go in the middle of the night.

00:05:51.120 --> 00:05:54.850
Why do I have to be the
only one carrying this big bag?!

00:05:54.920 --> 00:05:58.380
Yeah! We're not
common girls like YOU are!

00:05:59.390 --> 00:06:00.720
Who's common?!

00:06:00.790 --> 00:06:04.790
Never mind. I doubt any
ghosts'll be out in the morning...

00:06:04.860 --> 00:06:07.460
...so we'll just pop in and check
for the Claire Bible really fast.

00:06:07.530 --> 00:06:08.590
In that case...

00:06:10.670 --> 00:06:12.570
...you'll have no
complaints, right?

00:06:25.120 --> 00:06:27.450
Well... What do you know?

00:06:27.520 --> 00:06:29.490
Definitely a high
creep factor in here...

00:06:29.560 --> 00:06:30.920
Oh? Are you scared?

00:06:30.990 --> 00:06:32.690
N- No way!

00:06:32.760 --> 00:06:33.820
However...

00:06:33.890 --> 00:06:35.360
...you've got goose pimples.

00:06:56.120 --> 00:06:59.920
Damn! How could I let myself
get carried away like that?!

00:06:59.990 --> 00:07:02.950
Why are you making
excuses for yourself?

00:07:04.260 --> 00:07:09.060
Look, Xellos... That story
you told us. How old is it?

00:07:09.130 --> 00:07:12.390
Let's see...
Several hundred years, I believe.

00:07:12.800 --> 00:07:17.290
And the spell's still in effect?
That's the only explanation I have.

00:07:17.870 --> 00:07:21.570
Meaning the system amplifying the
curse must be incredibly powerful.

00:07:21.640 --> 00:07:25.300
So, you mean, that story about all
the people who entered the tower...

00:07:25.380 --> 00:07:28.310
...and getting turned
into dolls is true?

00:07:28.380 --> 00:07:31.820
The question is how to get into the
tower to look for the manuscript...

00:07:31.880 --> 00:07:33.880
...without making
all those dolls angry.

00:07:33.950 --> 00:07:38.150
Maybe that's why the man at
the inn gave us these to take.

00:07:42.090 --> 00:07:43.650
I REFUSE!

00:07:43.730 --> 00:07:47.030
I absolutely refuse to do
something this ridiculous!

00:07:47.100 --> 00:07:49.260
Well, great, except that
there's no other way to do this!

00:07:49.330 --> 00:07:51.000
Now quit being so selfish!

00:07:51.270 --> 00:07:53.700
Besides, everyone refused
to wear them at first...

00:07:53.770 --> 00:07:57.400
...but they're all enjoying
themselves now. See?

00:07:57.580 --> 00:08:02.040
My, I think that starfish suits
you well, Miss Amelia!

00:08:02.110 --> 00:08:03.880
It's not a starfish!

00:08:03.950 --> 00:08:07.390
This is the shining star
of love, hope, and Justice!

00:08:07.450 --> 00:08:11.250
Oh, you're so lucky!
What should I wear?

00:08:11.320 --> 00:08:14.690
Ah... I feel so comfortable
for some reason...

00:08:15.660 --> 00:08:17.630
Ridiculous...

00:08:17.700 --> 00:08:20.720
I don't care if the others
can do this. I can't!

00:08:20.800 --> 00:08:22.700
This is a question of policy!

00:08:22.770 --> 00:08:25.400
Oh... Well, guess that's that.

00:08:25.470 --> 00:08:28.630
I guess you don't mind letting Xellos
get to the book first, huh?

00:08:29.270 --> 00:08:31.140
I... I can't allow that!

00:08:31.880 --> 00:08:35.240
Well, if you can't, here!
You'll only be embarrassed once.

00:08:35.310 --> 00:08:37.610
Come on! Wear it!

00:08:39.450 --> 00:08:42.180
I see.
The effect is canceled.

00:08:42.250 --> 00:08:45.490
Apparently the dolls don't
consider us enemies now. However...

00:08:45.560 --> 00:08:48.750
...why do I have to
wear this stupid thing?!

00:08:48.830 --> 00:08:50.730
Okay!

00:08:50.800 --> 00:08:53.820
How do things look over
on your end, Mr. Bunny?

00:08:53.900 --> 00:08:57.100
Right... Nothing, so far.
And by the way...

00:08:57.170 --> 00:08:59.400
...would you PLEASE
stop calling me Mr. Bunny?!

00:08:59.470 --> 00:09:02.840
Oh? Why? I think it
suits you, Mr. Zelga-Bunny.

00:09:02.910 --> 00:09:04.600
Listen you!!!!

00:09:04.680 --> 00:09:07.670
I haven't found
anything like it, either.

00:09:08.410 --> 00:09:09.810
How about you, Amelia?

00:09:09.880 --> 00:09:12.180
I can't use my
hands in this getup!

00:09:12.250 --> 00:09:13.410
Oh, right...

00:09:13.490 --> 00:09:15.480
You really are stupid!

00:09:15.550 --> 00:09:18.250
You should dress in a useful
costume, like I have!

00:09:18.320 --> 00:09:20.190
Would you put a lid
on that ego already?!

00:09:22.190 --> 00:09:26.030
Ooh! I'm surrounded by idiots!
Are you really serious about this?!

00:09:26.100 --> 00:09:28.460
How can you say that
with what you're wearing?

00:09:29.970 --> 00:09:34.030
I wish one of these dolls at least
had a clue for finding the thing!

00:09:34.110 --> 00:09:37.910
Oh? You're looking
for a special doll?

00:09:37.980 --> 00:09:41.710
Yeah, but how can I find
anything with so many of them?

00:09:46.690 --> 00:09:50.490
Today I welcome you to
Joe and Anne's tower of dolls.

00:09:51.060 --> 00:09:54.650
Look, Anne. We have
guests after all this time.

00:09:54.890 --> 00:09:59.260
That's impossible! That story was
hundreds of years old, right?!

00:09:59.360 --> 00:10:02.390
No normal human can live that long!

00:10:03.340 --> 00:10:11.830
Unless... The man in the story used
a Monster's power to get the girl.

00:10:12.240 --> 00:10:14.970
You're saying... You made a
contract with a Monster?!

00:10:15.050 --> 00:10:17.380
Or did you use the
power of the Claire Bible?!

00:10:17.450 --> 00:10:21.650
Oh... You, too, came here
looking for the Claire Bible.

00:10:22.350 --> 00:10:25.450
Isn't that amusing, Anne?

00:10:31.260 --> 00:10:32.490
Very well!

00:10:32.560 --> 00:10:37.500
If you can get past the
four obstacles I've prepared...

00:10:37.570 --> 00:10:40.370
...and get to the
top floor of this tower...

00:10:40.440 --> 00:10:43.370
...then I will give
you what you seek.

00:10:43.440 --> 00:10:44.310
What?!

00:10:44.380 --> 00:10:45.310
Hey! Wait!

00:10:45.380 --> 00:10:48.540
However, the price
will be very high...

00:10:49.150 --> 00:10:53.350
It will be your lives!

00:11:09.030 --> 00:11:12.520
I never figured a Monster
would be mixed up in this, too.

00:11:12.600 --> 00:11:15.800
What'll we do, Miss Lina?
This has to be trap!

00:11:15.870 --> 00:11:19.600
I know it is! But as long as we
don't know for sure if...

00:11:19.670 --> 00:11:21.900
...the Claire Bible's in here or not,
we can't just run away screaming!

00:11:21.970 --> 00:11:25.210
We've gotta see
this through to the end!

00:11:37.120 --> 00:11:39.720
Hmpf! Choose someone
to be your representative!

00:11:39.790 --> 00:11:41.520
The first challenge shall be...

00:11:41.590 --> 00:11:43.150
...a cooking battle with me!

00:11:43.860 --> 00:11:45.890
A cooking battle?
Are you serious?

00:11:45.970 --> 00:11:47.930
Meaning it'll be no
trouble beating this...

00:11:48.000 --> 00:11:50.800
...stupid challenge and
going to the next one.

00:11:50.870 --> 00:11:52.200
Exactly!

00:11:52.270 --> 00:11:57.300
We've got three girls with us!
There's no way we can lose!

00:11:57.380 --> 00:11:59.810
Exactly! Piece of cake!

00:11:59.880 --> 00:12:04.010
And if you lose, Lord Joe's
magic will turn you into a doll!

00:12:04.650 --> 00:12:06.580
Better be careful!

00:12:06.650 --> 00:12:08.710
Uh... Yeah!
Better be careful, Amelia!

00:12:11.260 --> 00:12:13.490
We believe in you, Miss Martina!

00:12:13.560 --> 00:12:17.430
All right, then! I'll be cheering
you on with all my heart...

00:12:17.500 --> 00:12:18.360
...Master Xellos!

00:12:18.430 --> 00:12:20.400
HUH?! Me?!

00:12:24.140 --> 00:12:26.100
Victory is already in sight!

00:12:33.350 --> 00:12:37.980
I may have been pushed into this,
but don't underestimate my power!

00:12:40.150 --> 00:12:41.950
Wow! He's great!

00:12:42.020 --> 00:12:44.320
lm... Impressive!

00:12:47.660 --> 00:12:49.960
All done. Perfect!

00:12:50.030 --> 00:12:51.960
He's fast!

00:12:53.070 --> 00:12:55.190
Well, let's have a look.

00:13:07.380 --> 00:13:08.900
I may... just... die...

00:13:08.980 --> 00:13:10.510
Can't... take it...

00:13:11.880 --> 00:13:12.710
The smell!

00:13:12.790 --> 00:13:15.250
One bite can slay
even a golden dragon!

00:13:15.320 --> 00:13:17.290
The ultimate secret recipe!

00:13:17.360 --> 00:13:20.620
Mandragora soup
flavored with lamb chaos!

00:13:20.890 --> 00:13:23.190
Don't make stuff
we can't even identify!

00:13:23.260 --> 00:13:26.890
Well, it doesn't matter.
You've lost in any case!

00:13:31.500 --> 00:13:34.060
Xellos! And Martina!

00:13:45.580 --> 00:13:49.450
Now, then!
Let the second challenge begin!

00:13:50.490 --> 00:13:53.080
What are we supposed to do now?

00:13:54.030 --> 00:13:55.860
You must challenge me in a duel!

00:13:57.360 --> 00:14:00.030
A duel, huh? Then I'm your man!

00:14:00.100 --> 00:14:03.970
Don't hold back. Rock, paper...

00:14:06.010 --> 00:14:09.530
Hold it. By "duel", you mean
play "rock, paper, scissors"?

00:14:09.610 --> 00:14:11.580
Hah! I see now!

00:14:11.640 --> 00:14:15.050
With your eight arms, you can do rock,
paper, AND scissors all at once!

00:14:15.110 --> 00:14:16.710
Wow! Unusually sharp for him!

00:14:16.780 --> 00:14:18.250
Damn! He figured it out!

00:14:18.320 --> 00:14:21.550
You fool! A jellyfish has far
more arms than you have!

00:14:21.620 --> 00:14:23.350
Let's go! Rock, paper!

00:14:23.420 --> 00:14:25.120
Grrr... Rock, paper...

00:14:25.190 --> 00:14:27.160
Agh! I messed up!

00:14:28.530 --> 00:14:29.490
Paper!

00:14:29.560 --> 00:14:32.050
Look! Look! You lose!

00:14:32.200 --> 00:14:34.130
Aw, man...

00:14:34.670 --> 00:14:35.660
Jellyfish brains!

00:14:52.380 --> 00:14:55.250
Oh... Now Mr. Gourry's
been reduced to this, too...

00:14:55.320 --> 00:14:58.120
I think... it was inevitable
with someone as stupid as him!

00:14:58.190 --> 00:15:01.490
Okay, we've made it this far!
What's the next test?!

00:15:05.630 --> 00:15:08.660
Heh... Looks like we get a
better opponent this time.

00:15:10.840 --> 00:15:13.810
This battle won't be an easy one!

00:15:14.470 --> 00:15:17.410
Your challenge here...
is the End Catcher battle!

00:15:17.480 --> 00:15:18.700
That...

00:15:18.780 --> 00:15:20.300
That word game?

00:15:20.380 --> 00:15:25.820
Oh, forget it... Enjoy yourself.
This is right up your alley, Zelgadis.

00:15:26.120 --> 00:15:27.450
Why me?!

00:15:27.520 --> 00:15:29.920
Zelgadis...
Are you sure you want to?

00:15:37.160 --> 00:15:38.690
What the heck is this?!

00:15:38.760 --> 00:15:42.890
That girl just nominated you for this.
First, you get to be the ogre.

00:15:43.170 --> 00:15:47.000
Ogre? I thought the third
challenge was playing End Catcher!

00:15:47.070 --> 00:15:48.970
It IS End Catcher!

00:15:49.040 --> 00:15:52.170
When he catches hold of somebody
else's end, THEY become the ogre!

00:15:52.240 --> 00:15:56.340
The last person caught wearing
the ogre pants is the loser!

00:15:56.580 --> 00:15:58.350
But you don't HAVE
a butt for us to grab!

00:15:58.420 --> 00:15:59.280
That's cheating!

00:15:59.350 --> 00:16:01.840
Well, if you don't
want to be a doll...

00:16:01.920 --> 00:16:04.580
...you'd better grab
somebody else's end!

00:16:04.860 --> 00:16:07.420
Somebody else's... Hey!

00:16:10.160 --> 00:16:13.430
No... No...
Don't do it, Mr. Zelgadis...

00:16:13.870 --> 00:16:18.000
Now look! No, that won't work.
Maybe I can get Lina's...

00:16:18.300 --> 00:16:20.900
I think you know what'll
happen if you try THAT!

00:16:21.170 --> 00:16:26.340
Oh, great! So what am I
supposed to do?! This... This...

00:16:28.580 --> 00:16:30.170
This can't be!

00:16:36.090 --> 00:16:38.850
Oh... Mr. Zelgadis, I'm sorry!

00:16:38.920 --> 00:16:41.760
Okay, only one challenge left.

00:16:43.800 --> 00:16:46.700
Gotta pick which
door is the right one!

00:16:46.770 --> 00:16:49.600
Okay, I'll take the left side!

00:17:00.580 --> 00:17:03.450
What, this is
the final challenge?

00:17:03.520 --> 00:17:06.950
Ooh... Can't you think
of fairer traps to use?!

00:17:08.150 --> 00:17:10.210
Oh, wonderful! Just wonderful!

00:17:10.290 --> 00:17:12.720
I haven't had this
much fun in ages!

00:17:12.790 --> 00:17:15.990
What's wonderful about it?!
What are you up to, anyway?!

00:17:16.360 --> 00:17:25.270
Oh, nothing much. My strategy was
to lure you here with that old story...

00:17:25.340 --> 00:17:27.330
...Lina Inverse.

00:17:27.410 --> 00:17:29.070
Are you saying... You're a?!

00:17:29.140 --> 00:17:33.170
Yes! An honest to goodness,
living and breathing Monster.

00:17:33.610 --> 00:17:35.440
Isn't that right, Anne?

00:17:35.510 --> 00:17:38.640
I put on a good
performance, didn't I?

00:17:40.190 --> 00:17:44.880
So, that talk about the Claire
Bible manuscript being in a doll...

00:17:44.960 --> 00:17:46.980
A lie, naturally!

00:17:47.060 --> 00:17:50.520
You wouldn't have tried
so hard if I told you the truth.

00:17:51.330 --> 00:17:52.350
Well, that's true...

00:17:52.430 --> 00:17:57.370
Honestly, I didn't think catching
you would be so EASY!

00:17:58.640 --> 00:18:00.970
That stupid Xellos!

00:18:01.340 --> 00:18:03.830
But now that I know this,
I don't have to hold back!

00:18:03.910 --> 00:18:05.670
Elmekia Lance!

00:18:10.520 --> 00:18:14.540
You really think THAT
is enough to kill me?

00:18:18.090 --> 00:18:21.490
Damn! Astral Plane
attacks don't work on him!

00:18:22.530 --> 00:18:28.130
Unlike ordinary Monsters,
I am immortal!

00:18:33.240 --> 00:18:36.670
I see... Suddenly,
I'm all out of jokes to tell.

00:18:40.610 --> 00:18:43.270
Uh-oh... I still haven't
finished this recovery spell.

00:18:43.350 --> 00:18:46.010
I can't believe this guy
has me in such a tight pinch!

00:18:48.190 --> 00:18:48.850
Uh-oh!

00:18:50.560 --> 00:18:53.050
And now, it's all over!

00:18:57.900 --> 00:18:58.560
Xellos?!

00:18:58.630 --> 00:19:03.660
Oh, my, I'm so embarrassed.
Being tricked by that story like that.

00:19:04.140 --> 00:19:08.230
You should be, especially since we
came here because of your information!

00:19:08.310 --> 00:19:12.070
I was thinking about that
while I was turned into a doll.

00:19:12.140 --> 00:19:13.770
So?! What took you
so long to think about?

00:19:13.850 --> 00:19:16.040
When I thought about
puppet-using Monsters...

00:19:16.110 --> 00:19:19.480
...I remembered an old
acquaintance of mine.

00:19:20.650 --> 00:19:22.640
Acquaintance?

00:19:26.830 --> 00:19:30.850
One who uses puppets to distract her
enemies from where she REALLY is.

00:19:34.530 --> 00:19:35.190
Lina!

00:19:35.270 --> 00:19:37.760
Gotcha! Elmekia Lance!

00:19:43.110 --> 00:19:48.670
You see, in reality, the man
was actually the puppet.

00:19:48.750 --> 00:19:50.040
I get you...

00:19:50.120 --> 00:19:52.410
Damn you...
Damn you, Xellos!

00:19:53.120 --> 00:19:56.280
All right, Lina. You can
cut loose without any worries.

00:19:56.360 --> 00:19:57.320
Okay!

00:19:57.390 --> 00:20:00.690
"Darkness beyond twilight,
crimson beyond blood that flows..."

00:20:00.760 --> 00:20:02.850
Et cetera, et cetera!

00:20:02.930 --> 00:20:06.490
DRAGON SLAVE!!!

00:20:18.540 --> 00:20:21.540
So, "all's well that
ends well," right?

00:20:21.610 --> 00:20:26.450
Ends well HOW? This whole
stupid mess was all your fault!

00:20:26.520 --> 00:20:31.820
Please! Didn't I save you from
that tight pinch you were in?

00:20:31.890 --> 00:20:34.050
Which is something
I STILL don't understand!

00:20:34.130 --> 00:20:37.060
Why were you the only
one immune to the spell?!

00:20:37.130 --> 00:20:40.360
And how was that
Monster an "acquaintance"?!

00:20:40.430 --> 00:20:42.800
Well, to end this discussion...

00:20:43.800 --> 00:20:45.790
I apologize.

00:20:49.040 --> 00:20:52.410
Ah... I'm really
getting hooked on this...

00:20:54.510 --> 00:20:57.180
What's the meaning
of my existence?

00:20:57.250 --> 00:20:59.180
To be a convenient
lackey for Lina? No...

00:20:59.250 --> 00:21:00.510
I'm supposed to be a
heartless swordsman.

00:21:00.590 --> 00:21:03.280
A bit dark and mysterious,
but that doesn't mean...
